# UAE E-Invoice Test Framework

Playwright + TypeScript E2E automation with Python (openpyxl) for Excel generation.

## Layer boundaries (do not blur these)

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| Specs | `tests/` | Scenarios, data loops, expected outcomes only — no raw selectors |
| Fixture | `Src/baseTest.ts` | Session bootstrap, worker identity, attachments, cleanup, site-unavailable skip |
| Page Objects | `pageObjects/` | Locators, UI actions, resilient waits only |
| Helpers | `Helpers/` | Business flows (upload, submit, field/formula/UI validation orchestration) |
| Utils | `utils/` | Python bridge, Excel generation, global setup, env/config |
| Test data | `testData/` | Datasets, template headers, static uploads |

## Non-negotiables

- Import `test` from `Src/baseTest.ts` — never directly from `@playwright/test` in specs.
- Generated workbooks go to worker-isolated paths: `testData/generated/excel/pw-<index>/`.
- Never commit `.env`, `storageState.json`, or report artifacts (`allure-results/`, `playwright-report/`).
- Two Excel pipelines — do not mix without understanding:
  - `generateInvoiceExcel` → formula/min-max field validation (camelCase payload)
  - `generateInvoiceFromSubmitData` → submit-shaped rows (Excel header keys); totals are recalculated
- UI specs (`UI*.spec.ts`, `UIMaster*.spec.ts`) run under `chromium-ui` project; upload specs use `chromium`.

## Parallel safety

- Default 5 workers map to TIN slots 1779700001–1779700005.
- Use worker identity helpers (`parallelWorkerSubmitIdentity.ts`, `UAE_EINVOICE_WORKER_INDEX`).
- Do not hardcode invoice numbers that can collide across workers.

